This is an arugula salad on a square white plate, probably about 24 cm across. The greens cover roughly 10 x 14 cm in a loose pile. Arugula is very light, so I estimate about 40 g. A few small brown bits look like nuts or bacon, and the leaves seem to have a light coat of dressing. I add about 5 g for the bits and about 8 g for the dressing, which brings the total to roughly 50 g.

For energy, 40 g of arugula is about 10 kcal. The dressing, at roughly 1 tablespoon of oil-based vinaigrette, adds about 60 kcal. The nuts or bacon add about 20 kcal. That gives roughly 90 kcal in total.

